From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: airoha: only enable STAG for the DSA conduit

airoha_dev_open() enabled GDM_STAG_EN for any port with id > 2 as well as
for the DSA conduit.  lan1 is gdm3, which connects directly to the
EN8811H PHY and never passes through the switch, so enabling the switch
special tag there makes the driver expect switch tagging and drops every
frame: the interface reports carrier and correct link speed but both RX
and TX counters stay at zero.

Upstream 6.18 keys this purely off netdev_uses_dsa().

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-10 08:31:26.891649768 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-10 08:31:26.895650180 +0800
@@ -1928,8 +1928,13 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	/* It seems GDM3 and GDM4 needs SPORT enabled to correctly work */
-	if (netdev_uses_dsa(dev) || port->id > 2)
+	/* Only the DSA conduit needs the special tag.  lan1 is gdm3, which
+	 * is wired straight to the EN8811H and does not pass through the
+	 * switch, so enabling STAG there makes the driver expect switch
+	 * tagging and every frame is dropped (RX/TX stay at zero).
+	 * Upstream (6.18) keys this purely off netdev_uses_dsa().
+	 */
+	if (netdev_uses_dsa(dev))
 		airoha_fe_set(qdma->eth, REG_GDM_INGRESS_CFG(port->id),
 			      GDM_STAG_EN_MASK);
 	else
